<section class="hero">
<div class="wrap">
<span class="eyebrow">Cluster — 48-hour response</span>
<h1>Furniture inspection &amp; supplier verification in Moradabad</h1>
<p class="lead">The metalware capital: Moradabad's furniture manufacturers work in iron, aluminium and metal-wood combination furniture and hardware. Every Qualis service is available across the cluster now, with 48-hour response.</p>
<div class="hero-ctas"><a class="btn btn-solid" href="/#book">Book an inspection</a><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/why-independent/">Why independent</a></div>
</div>
</section>
<section><div class="wrap"><h2 class="vh">What we inspect in Moradabad</h2><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/pre-shipment-inspection-india/"><h3>Weld quality</h3><p>Ground-and-painted welds hide porosity and cold joints; structural checks and load tests catch what paint covers.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/defects/"><h3>Coating adhesion</h3><p>Powder-coat and plating failures show up as rust complaints months later — adhesion and film checks at PSI prevent them.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/pre-shipment-inspection-india/"><h3>Metal-wood interfaces</h3><p>Mixed-material joints loosen with wood movement; fastener and insert checks are cluster-standard here.</p></a></div></div></section><section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>What Moradabad makes, and why buyers source here</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">Moradabad is the metalware capital — long known as India’s &ldquo;Brass City&rdquo; — and the one cluster on this list where the core material is not wood. Its furniture manufacturers work in iron, aluminium and metal-wood combination pieces, plus the bases, frames and hardware that ship on to factories elsewhere, often mated with Jodhpur wood tops. That changes what an inspection is about: moisture and timber grading recede, and weld integrity, coating and plating durability, and the behaviour of mixed-material joints move to the front.</p><p class="prose rv">The failure modes are different, and so is the checklist. A ground-and-painted weld can hide porosity or a cold joint that no amount of finish inspection would catch; powder-coat and plating that pass on the day can fail months later as rust complaints from the destination; and metal-wood joints loosen as the wood component moves in a drier climate. A buyer used to inspecting solid-wood furniture should expect Moradabad to be checked against a metalware standard, not a timber one.</p></div></section><section><div class="wrap"><div class="grid"><a class="card rv" href="/pre-shipment-inspection-india/"><h3>Pre-Shipment Inspection</h3><p>AQL 2.5, moisture, structure, finish vs golden sample — report in 24h.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/supplier-verification-india/"><h3>Supplier Verification</h3><p>Unannounced premises visits, verdict in 3–5 working days.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/factory-audit-india/"><h3>Factory Audit</h3><p>8-section scored audit for programme onboarding.</p></a><a class="card rv" href="/container-loading-supervision/"><h3>Container Loading Supervision</h3><p>Tally, dunnage, weather hold and photographed seal.</p></a></div></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>How Qualis covers Moradabad</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">Moradabad is covered on a 48-hour response from our Jodhpur base. Its defining risks are the ones paint hides, which is why they are checked with structural and adhesion tests at pre-shipment rather than by eye — weld integrity and load behaviour, coating and plating film and adhesion, and fastener and insert checks on every mixed metal-wood joint. Every Qualis service runs here — pre-shipment inspection, supplier verification, factory audit and container loading supervision — buyer-paid, with a photographed report inside 24 hours of the visit.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><div class="sec-head"><div><h2>Before you order from Moradabad</h2></div></div><p class="prose rv">A metalware order rewards a few decisions made up front. <strong>Specify the coating standard, not just the colour</strong> — powder-coat and plating failures surface months later as rust complaints, so put the coating and adhesion expectation in the PO and check film and adhesion at pre-shipment. <strong>Treat welds as a structural spec</strong> — ground-and-painted welds hide porosity and cold joints, so agree load and structural expectations that can be tested rather than eyeballed. <strong>Scope in the metal-wood joints</strong> — mixed-material joints loosen as the wood moves in a drier climate, so fastener and insert checks belong in the inspection from the first order.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap prose-wrap"><p class="prose rv"><strong>Where Moradabad containers land.</strong> The same goods fail differently by destination — climate sets the moisture specification and the market sets the paperwork. Read the guide for <a href="/importing-furniture-from-india/usa/">the USA</a>, <a href="/importing-furniture-from-india/uk/">the UK</a>, <a href="/importing-furniture-from-india/germany/">Germany</a> and <a href="/importing-furniture-from-india/canada/">Canada</a>, or the full <a href="/importing-furniture-from-india/">set of ten market guides</a>.</p></div></section>
